CX Intake → XDI: Minimal Metadata & ID Guide (v1.0)
Scope: This document locks the minimum viable metadata (MVM) and IDs from raw intake to the XDI-ready flattened 
ED rows, including when/where each field is attached and how artifacts are merged.
Out of scope: Post‑XDI PDCA/Outcome/PEM. (We stop at OU creation/clustering readiness.)

1) Canonical Flow (LOCKED)
A. RAW INTAKE (attach Layer‑0: Intake & Lineage) → one row per source message
B. UNPACK (operate only on raw_text) → produce unwrapped_cx_block (multi‑ED markdown)
C. MERGE (join A + B by dedupe_key) → single message-level record with metadata + unwrapped block
D. PARSE & FLATTEN (atomic unit = Experience Driver) → one row per ED with: ED fields, IDs, time splits; 
duplicates Layer‑0 metadata onto every ED row → XDI‑ready

2) Layer‑0: Intake & Lineage (LOCKED minimal set)
Attach at RAW INTAKE. Remains immutable and is duplicated to each ED row during PARSE & FLATTEN.


Why only these? They provide provenance, replayability, and idempotency without bloat.

