Rule: Do not mutate or duplicate Layer‑0 metadata here. Keep unpack lineage separate until MERGE.

4) Merge (message‑level)
Join A + B by dedupe_key to produce one record per message with:
Layer‑0 metadata + raw_text + unwrapped_cx_block (+ unpack lineage).
This artifact is the input to PARSE & FLATTEN.

5) Parse & Flatten (ED‑level; XDI‑ready)
Goal: Produce one row per Experience Driver found in unwrapped_cx_block.
Carry‑through: Duplicate all Layer‑0 fields to each ED row.
Add only inevitable ED IDs + time splits.

  5.1 ED Fields (from the current parser)
- experience_driver, entity_name, theme, context
- feedback_type (canonical 7), customer_effort_score
- emotion → derived: emotion_primary, emotion_specific
- Journey location: customer_journey, customer_journey_stage, interaction_moment 
- Action lane: opportunity_stream (Fix/Optimize/Amplify/Innovate), ou_name
- Semantics: semantic_action_statement → derived splits: semantic_customer_reality, semantic_strategic_response
- matters, stream_justification, behavioral_impact, keywords[]

5.2 IDs (inevitable & minimal)
ed_id — canonical Experience Driver ID
 • Provisional at parse time: stable hash of normalized (theme|experience_driver)
 • Later promotion to registry keeps this field; track: ed_id_origin = provisional|registry, ed_registry_version (optional)

ed_row_id — occurrence ID for this ED row
 • Deterministic hash of dedupe_key + ED tuple (experience_driver|entity_name|context|feedback_type|opportunity_stream|customer_journey|customer_journey_stage|interaction_moment)

We intentionally avoid extra IDs. No additional keys unless required by registry adoption later 
(e.g., optional entity_registry_id).

5.3 Time Splits (for XDI rollups)
- timestamp_utc — from event_timestamp normalized to UTC; fallback ingest_timestamp
- date_local, time_local — derived using event_timezone (fallback: tenant/site default)

5.4 Idempotency (ED‑level)
- ed_row_id serves as row‑level idempotency (supersedes any separate row_dedupe_key).


6) Join Keys & Duplication Rules
- Primary join unit: dedupe_key (message level).
Fallback: (record_id,thread_id,message_index) only when necessary.

- Duplication: All Layer‑0 fields must be duplicated to every ED row. This is what gives ED‑level 
lineage and auditability.


7) Artifact Naming (suggested)
- intake_raw_messages — RAW INTAKE table/file (immutable)
- intake_unwrapped — UNPACK outputs keyed by dedupe_key
- prexdi_messages — MERGE of raw+unwrapped (message‑level)
- xdi_ready_ed_flat — PARSE & FLATTEN output (ED‑level; compute‑ready)


8) Minimal Deterministic Recipes
# Provisional ED ID (stable across runs pre‑registry)
ed_id = 'ed:' + sha256( lower(norm(theme)) + '|' + lower(norm(experience_driver)) )[:16]

# ED row occurrence ID (idempotency at ED granularity)
ed_tuple = join('|', norm(experience_driver), norm(entity_name), norm(context),
                      norm(feedback_type), norm(opportunity_stream),
                      norm(customer_journey), norm(customer_journey_stage),
                      norm(interaction_moment))
ed_row_id = 'edrow:' + sha256( dedupe_key + '|' + ed_tuple )[:24]

# Time splits
if event_timestamp has offset -> to UTC
else -> assume event_timezone (or tenant default) then to UTC
=> timestamp_utc, plus date_local/time_local via event_timezone

norm() uses your existing text normalization: Unicode NFKC → strip ZWCs → arrow canon → space canon → trim.

9) Validation Checklist (before XDI)
- Every message has Layer‑0 fields populated (at least required ones).
- Every ED row duplicates Layer‑0 fields.
- ed_id present (provisional allowed), ed_row_id present.
- timestamp_utc present; date_local & time_local derived.
- No duplicate ED rows for same message (ed_row_id uniqueness holds).
- Parser output stored as xdi_ready_ed_flat and ready for Layer‑2/3 compute.

Summary (why this is minimal and sufficient)
- Traceability: tenant/environment + source pointers + fingerprints.
- Idempotency: message‑level dedupe_key and ED‑level ed_row_id.
- Determinism: provisional ed_id + normalized hashing.
- Compute‑ready: time splits and ED fields required for OU selection/clustering.

No extra IDs. No speculative fields. Just what’s necessary to keep the pipeline transparent, reproducible, 
and ready for action.


