10.3 ID Recipe (Deterministic)
# Canonical text signature for this PS
ps_signature = sha256( lower(norm(problem_statement_text)) )[:16]


# Deterministic ID for this PS version
ps_id = 'ps:' + sha256( ou_id + '|' + pipeline_run_id + '|' + ps_signature )[:24]

(Use the same norm()/canonicalization as earlier to avoid drift.)

10.4 Reconciliation Flow (Minimal)
1. Generate PS from OU context (header + membership snapshot). Save as ps_status='draft'.
2. Optional edit by human. If edited, update problem_statement_text, set authored_by='human', editor_user_id, edit_timestamp. Recompute ps_id (text changed ⇒ new signature) and set ps_status='approved' when accepted.
3. Bind to OU: Write ps_current_id = <approved ps_id> back to xdi_ou_header for that (ou_id, pipeline_run_id).
4. Supersede on change: If OU membership or cluster signature changes in a later run, a new OU instance will exist (same ou_id, different pipeline_run_id). A new PS will be generated/approved for that instance.

This keeps OU⇄PS linkage deterministic, traceable, and minimal—no extra instance IDs, no bloat.

